# Production environment — faculty instance

Copy to the instance root as `.env` on the server.  
Replace every `CHANGE_ME` value. Never commit a real production `.env`.

```ini
CI_ENVIRONMENT = production

app.baseURL = 'https://fseg.CHANGE_ME.edu/'
app.defaultLocale = fr
app.appTimezone = Africa/Bujumbura
app.forceGlobalSecureRequests = true
app.CSPEnabled = true

app.siteSlug = fseg
app.centralAdminMode = false
app.defaultSiteSlug =
app.allowedHostnames = fseg.CHANGE_ME.edu
app.requireKnownHostname = true

# {slug} is replaced when running php spark site:create.
# Alwaysdata: {slug}.ACCOUNT.alwaysdata.net
# Own domain: {slug}.ub.edu.bi
app.publicHostPattern = {slug}.CHANGE_ME.edu

database.default.hostname = localhost
database.default.database = ub_shared
database.default.username = ubapp
database.default.password = CHANGE_ME_STRONG_DB_PASSWORD
database.default.DBDriver = MySQLi
database.default.DBPrefix =
database.default.port = 3306
database.default.DBDebug = false

# Keep tests off production servers. If present, use a throwaway DB name only.
database.tests.hostname = localhost
database.tests.database = ub_shared_test_UNUSED
database.tests.username = ubapp
database.tests.password = CHANGE_ME_STRONG_DB_PASSWORD
database.tests.DBDriver = MySQLi
database.tests.DBPrefix = test_
database.tests.port = 3306

CONTACT_NOTIFICATION_ENABLED = false
CONTACT_NOTIFICATION_RECIPIENT = contact@CHANGE_ME.edu
CONTACT_NOTIFICATION_FROM_EMAIL = no-reply@CHANGE_ME.edu
CONTACT_NOTIFICATION_FROM_NAME = FSEG
CONTACT_NOTIFICATION_PROTOCOL = smtp
CONTACT_NOTIFICATION_SMTP_HOST = smtp.CHANGE_ME.edu
CONTACT_NOTIFICATION_SMTP_PORT = 587
CONTACT_NOTIFICATION_SMTP_CRYPTO = tls
CONTACT_NOTIFICATION_SMTP_USER = CHANGE_ME
CONTACT_NOTIFICATION_SMTP_PASS = CHANGE_ME

# Generate on the server: php spark key:generate
encryption.key = CHANGE_ME_RUN_php_spark_key_generate

session.cookieName = ci_session_fseg
session.rememberCookieName = remember_fseg

# Leave empty on faculty instances (unless you know you need mirrors).
# app.uploadMirrors =

# Only if PHP sits behind a reverse proxy / load balancer you trust:
# app.proxyIPs = 10.0.0.1
```

## Per-faculty cookie names

| Folder | `app.siteSlug` | `session.cookieName` | `session.rememberCookieName` |
|--------|----------------|----------------------|------------------------------|
| fseg | fseg | ci_session_fseg | remember_fseg |
| fsi | fsi | ci_session_fsi | remember_fsi |
| med | med | ci_session_med | remember_med |
| fabi | fabi | ci_session_fabi | remember_fabi |
| flsh | flsh | ci_session_flsh | remember_flsh |

## After writing `.env`

```bash
php spark key:generate
php spark app:production-check
php spark app:production-check --strict
```

Blocking issues must be fixed before go-live. See [09-production-go-live.md](09-production-go-live.md).
